# TrainGrid environment variables.
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development. Never commit real values:
# .env, .env.local and every other .env.* file are ignored by Git.
#
# Local development points at the local Supabase stack (npm run supabase:start),
# never at the production project. Production values live only in
# Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables (Production).

# --- Public: sent to the browser by design -----------------------------------
# Safety comes from Supabase Auth and Row Level Security, not from hiding these.

# Local stack: http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321

# Publishable key (starts with sb_publishable_). For the local stack, copy it
# from the output of: npm run supabase:status
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-key

# --- Server only: must never reach the browser --------------------------------
# Not needed until the admin invitation flow. Leave unset until then.

# Secret key (starts with sb_secret_). Bypasses Row Level Security.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Comma-separated Supabase user ids allowed to manage invitations.
# TRAINGRID_ADMIN_USER_IDS=
